.Dd May 18, 2026
.Dt USERADD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm useradd
.Nd create a new user account
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl u Ar UID Op Fl o
.Op Fl g Ar GROUP
.Op Fl G Ar LIST
.Op Fl d Ar HOMEDIR
.Op Fl s Ar SHELL
.Op Fl c Ar COMMENT
.Op Fl m
.Op Fl M
.Op Fl N
.Op Fl r
.Ar USER
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
adds a new user entry to
.Pa /etc/passwd
and a matching locked-account row to
.Pa /etc/shadow .
By default it also creates a per-user group with the same name as
.Ar USER
(by spawning
.Xr groupadd 8 )
and assigns it as the user's primary group; see
.Fl N
to override that behaviour.
.Pp
Database changes are atomic per file: each rewrite is built in
.Pa <file>.new ,
.Xr fsync 2 Ns 'd ,
then renamed over the original.
.Pa /etc/.pwd.lock
serialises against concurrent admin tools.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl u Ar UID
Use the supplied numeric user ID instead of auto-allocating.
Refuses to clobber an existing UID unless
.Fl o
is given.
.It Fl o
With
.Fl u ,
allow non-unique UIDs.
.It Fl g Ar GROUP
Primary group, named or numeric.  The group must already exist.
Implies
.Fl N
(no per-user group is created).
.It Fl G Ar LIST
Comma-separated supplementary group names.  Each group must already
exist;
.Nm
appends
.Ar USER
to every named group's member list.
.It Fl d Ar HOMEDIR
Home directory path recorded in
.Pa /etc/passwd .
Defaults to
.Pa /home/USER
for regular users and
.Pa /var/empty
for system accounts.
.It Fl s Ar SHELL
Login shell.  Default
.Pa /bin/sh ,
or
.Pa /bin/false
when
.Fl r
is in effect.
.It Fl c Ar COMMENT
GECOS field (full name / contact info).
.It Fl m
Create the home directory (mode 0700, owned by the new user).
.It Fl M
Do not create the home directory even if defaults would otherwise.
Accepted for parity with shadow-utils.
.It Fl N
Don't auto-create a per-user group; with
.Fl g
this is the default.
.It Fl r
System account.  Allocate UID/GID from
.Bq 1, 999 ,
default shell
.Pa /bin/false ,
home
.Pa /var/empty ,
do not create the home directory.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 2
Bad usage.
.It 3
Invalid argument value.
.It 4
UID already in use (without
.Fl o ) .
.It 6
A group named via
.Fl g
or
.Fl G
does not exist.
.It 9
.Ar USER
already exists.
.It 10
Failed to update
.Pa /etc/passwd .
.It 12
Failed to create the home directory.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa /etc/gshadow
.It Pa /etc/passwd
Account database.
.It Pa /etc/shadow
Password-hash database.
.It Pa /etc/group
Group database.
.It Pa /etc/gshadow
Group-password database (only updated if present).
.It Pa /etc/.pwd.lock
Cross-tool serialisation lock.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr fcntl 2 ,
.Xr getpwnam 3 ,
.Xr pwdb_lock 3 ,
.Xr passwd 5 ,
.Xr shadow 5 ,
.Xr groupadd 8 ,
.Xr userdel 8 ,
.Xr usermod 8
.Sh AUTHORS
Substrate-native
.Nm ,
written to match the shadow-utils command-line surface.
